<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>X3Code.Utilities</PackageId>
    <Product>X3Code.Utilities</Product>
    <Title>X3-Code Utilities</Title>
    <Description>Some little helpers for every project</Description>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>10.0.0: New version scheme - the major now tracks the .NET generation the package is built for (net10.0), the minor carries features and breaking changes, the patch carries fixes. All X3Code packages move to 10.0.0 together.
The package now ships its XML documentation, so consumers get IntelliSense. Added an MIT license expression, a README and a symbol package (snupkg) with SourceLink.
Fixed six malformed documentation links that used cref for external URLs instead of href (ArbitraryNumberConverter, RegexUtilities, MimeTypeConverter).
Microsoft.Data.SqlClient 6.1.4 -> 6.1.6.
All asynchronous methods on IBasicHttpClient/BasicHttpClient now take a CancellationToken. The parameter is optional, so existing call sites keep compiling.
Fixed: the generic GetAsync overload started a ReadAsStringAsync task that was never awaited and read the content stream in parallel with the deserialization.
Fixed: UploadStreamAsync never disposed its StreamContent.
BREAKING: DatabaseConnector moved out into its own package, X3Code.Sql.Utils, and into the X3Code.Sql.Utils namespace. It was the only type here that needed Microsoft.Data.SqlClient and pulled that whole graph - Azure.Identity, Microsoft.IdentityModel.*, the native SNI assets - into every consumer of this package. X3Code.Utilities now has no package dependencies at all.
DataRowExtension no longer casts the cell to string. Against a typed DataTable - which is what a database hands back - that threw an InvalidCastException, and it took ToInteger, ToDecimal, ToFloat, ToDouble, ToDateTime, ToBoolean and ToChar down with it. Typed columns are now read natively, so ToDateTime no longer needs a matching pattern for a real date column.
ToChar returns the documented '\0' for an empty column instead of throwing, and signals a too-long value with ArgumentException instead of a bare Exception.
EntityPropertyExtension formats with InvariantCulture. Previously a decimal came out as "42,42" on a machine with a German locale and as "42.42" elsewhere.
Argument checks throw ArgumentException with the parameter name instead of a bare Exception - BasicHttpClient (base URL, header, value, username, password, token), GuidTools.ReplaceGuidBlockWith and DictionaryExtension for a duplicate key. ConfigurationLoader now uses NotSupportedException for an unknown file extension and InvalidDataException for an empty or undeserializable file. Catching these on purpose is possible now; catching Exception was the only option before.
BREAKING: X3HttpRequestException carries the response body as a string plus the status code instead of the HttpResponseMessage. Holding the response meant holding an IDisposable that nobody disposed and that could already be gone when the exception was inspected. TryParseResponseContent is synchronous now, needs no network, and returns the default instead of throwing - which is what its name promised all along.
RomanianConverter validates its input: null raises ArgumentNullException, a character that is no roman numeral raises ArgumentException naming the character and its position instead of a bare KeyNotFoundException, and a negative number raises ArgumentOutOfRangeException instead of running into a negative array index.
Fixed: FillPlaceholderFromEntity replaced a placeholder whose property exists but holds null with the entire input string - "Hello %Nickname% World" came back as "Hello Hello %Nickname% World World". The placeholder is left standing now. A placeholder naming a property that does not exist still resolves to an empty string.
Removed: SoftwareEnvironmentExtension.ToString. An extension method always loses against the instance method of the same name, so it was unreachable through extension syntax - and it looked like an endless recursion.
New: optional logging through Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions. BasicHttpClient and ConfigurationLoader take an optional ILogger that defaults to NullLogger, so nothing changes for existing code. The HTTP client reports a failed request with its URI, status code and response body; the configuration loader reports the path a file was actually resolved to. The events are written with the LoggerMessage source generator, so a call costs nothing while the level is switched off.
This is the only package dependency of X3Code.Utilities. Logging.Abstractions carries no sink and no configuration - Serilog, NLog, OpenTelemetry or nothing at all remains entirely the application's decision.
BREAKING: the parameters of IConfigurationLoader.Load are declared as (fileName, pathToConfigFile) now, matching the implementation. They used to be the other way round on the interface only - a call through the interface with named arguments bound the two across, and the compiler could not see it because both are strings. Positional callers are unaffected. The interface also has XML documentation now.
Fixed: UploadStreamAsync closed the caller's stream. It wrapped the stream in a StreamContent and disposed that; StreamContent.Dispose disposes the stream it wraps. The response is disposed instead now.</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" />
  </ItemGroup>


</Project>
